      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 1,
      "q": "If $\\sin^{-1}x+\\cot^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$, then $x$ is equal to :",
      "options": [
        "$\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt5}$",
        "$\\dfrac12$",
        "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
        "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt5}$"
      ],
      "answer": 3,
      "solution": "$\\sin^{-1}x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}-\\cot^{-1}\\dfrac12=\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac12$. An angle with $\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac12$ has $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt5}$, so $x=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt5}$."
    },
